  "accepted_answers": [
    "April 1958"
  ],
  "explanation": "The question asks specifically for the start of construction of the 'Time-Life Building'. Source D1S2 explicitly states: 'Construction on the Time-Life Building's steelwork started in April 1958'. The alternative candidate 'June 1936' (from D2S2) refers to the excavation of a 'new building at 1 Rockefeller Plaza' (later identified as 9 Rockefeller Plaza), which is a different project or phase described in a separate context. While D2S4 mentions the original blueprints were retained for the Time & Life Building, it does not state that the 1936 excavation was the start of the Time-Life Building's construction itself. Therefore, only 'April 1958' directly answers the specific query regarding the Time-Life Building's construction start."
}
